## The Ultimate Bottleneck: Your Lifespan
While you can theoretically achieve bronze-working in a single lifetime if you are incredibly lucky with finding surface ores, your greatest limitation is knowledge transmission. Real technology accelerates exponentially because thousands of humans share, refine, and pass down data over generations. As a solitary human, your final and most important technology would be creating a written language—carving your discoveries onto stone tablets so that whoever comes after you doesn't have to reinvent the wheel.
